        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A group of galactosemias characterized by GALT deficiency and presenting with variable clinical features depending on the residual GALT activity present in affected individuals going from classic galactosemia manifesting with life-threatening complications triggered by breastfeeding or the ingestion of lactose/galactose-containing formula in untreated infants and long term-complications despite diet (GALT activity <1%) to a less severe phenotype (GALT activity 1-10%) or completely asymptomatic patients (GALT activity 25-30%)."
        },
